WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:06.822
Multiplying with negative numbers follows a pattern. First, two positive numbers.

00:06.822 --> 00:08.929
Three times four is twelve.

00:09.379 --> 00:15.997
Three times negative four means three groups of negative four. That is negative twelve.

00:16.447 --> 00:22.507
Negative three times four is also negative twelve. The order does not matter.

00:22.957 --> 00:30.689
And a negative times a negative is positive. Negative three times negative four is positive twelve.

00:31.139 --> 00:38.332
Here is the rule. If the signs are the same, the answer is positive. If the signs are different,

00:38.332 --> 00:40.056
the answer is negative.

00:40.506 --> 00:46.914
Dividing works the same way. Negative twelve divided by three is negative four.
